# Bundle-local re-inclusion rules.
#
# The umbrella .gitignore carries generic build-output rules that are correct
# for build output and wrong for retained qualification evidence. Without the
# negations below, 127 of this bundle's 217 files would sit in the working tree
# untracked -- as perishable as the ephemeral scratch directory this bundle
# exists to replace. The umbrella rules that actually match here are:
#
#   .gitignore:30  [Bb]in/     .gitignore:31  [Oo]bj/
#   .gitignore:32  [Ll]og/     .gitignore:33  [Ll]ogs/   -> 117 files under logs/
#   .gitignore:76  *.meta      .gitignore:92  *.log      -> 2 retained qualification.log
#   .gitignore:196 *.nupkg     .gitignore:198 *.snupkg   -> 8 retained G-4 packages
#
# `[Ll]ogs/` excludes the directory itself, so `!logs/` must precede `!logs/**`;
# a deeper .gitignore wins over a shallower one. `*.meta` is negated explicitly
# rather than left to survive incidentally through `!logs/**`, and `bin/`/`obj/`
# are negated so a future relocated lane artifact under such a path is kept.
# There is no umbrella `*.diag` rule today; `!*.diag` guards against one.
#
# Scope is this bundle only. No file outside it, and no earlier bundle, is
# affected.
!logs/
!logs/**
!*.log
!*.meta
!*.diag
!*.nupkg
!*.snupkg
!bin/
!bin/**
!obj/
!obj/**
